[{"id":"VRCE-2-56-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":56,"verse":1,"english":"Thus harshly addressed by the indignant mother of Rāma, the king aggrieved was plunged in thought. Having thought for a long while, that repressor of foes, the king, who had lost his senses through grief, regained consciousness.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-62-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2056001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b72d68fd48fdd91a50c846b2338d609cdd0aef5153961729c9292d59169aa8d7","compact":"369369ffb6addf7cdd4f809bd5614e9706263430af79060560c949af26147d6b","nasal":"a4365a030ce1bfb363f843ec4b9ef4bd10e126a7713b5f63cad8d7699c0421ea"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-56-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":56,"verse":2,"english":"As he was thinking, the sinful act which he had through ignorance formerly committed by means of the shaft which hits by sounds, rose up in his recollection,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-62-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2056002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2cc6985c1e78ef76f3fc59a7594af6f54273c62b0844f46dcc3ccc03768e5f6e","compact":"52c0d485bdd5f514b0cc9be8f75345a9eb4324f38f6f61733ba686edaea8d919","nasal":"abc8606020f2c56e687db3fc534f94af57a1efad27a5a24f99652fd5e0862f47"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-56-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":56,"verse":3,"english":"Afflicted with this grief as well as that on account of Rāma, that lord, the king, burned in these two several griefs. Burning in grief and distressed, he trembling and with joined hands, with his head hanging down, addressed Kausalyā, with the view of pacifying her.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.397,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-62-4","DUTT-2-62-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2056003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"acf6271aad5d66f42bce0104fa0d474a9a7b86bb1b7ea7ca3ff970a97ef8787c","compact":"30216888b729f98977b19edb9366ed5ec1777589f85e96865a3ff050307f2cd8","nasal":"30216888b729f98977b19edb9366ed5ec1777589f85e96865a3ff050307f2cd8"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-56-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":56,"verse":4,"english":"I deprecate your displeasure. O Kausalyä with joined hands. You are ever affectionate and did not treat harshly even enemies.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-62-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2056004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4386d3be50bd636357e2cce0ddac95ec25f258348fa811a8586a318f2dbc3b0e","compact":"a5bc14c859bcc6f94f7e06bc970f10ee2a593f65c6f75a836e8efd84e5179703","nasal":"47602edcbc3b00bd214b82a051a20e288d6f4a02f47d3eca126300a305f07aa6"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-56-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":56,"verse":5,"english":"Verily to women cognizant of virtue, a husband, whether he has any merits or not, is a very deity.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-62-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2056005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2e801ef232d180b836b44472d065ef303cac31b3b1de36c23fce90364c8587b0","compact":"04ea8083a49d63d0b31f8a6de42f2b1fa5dc3cea00c1f5f2bf3e2894a4122205","nasal":"d19713b0d5142f51f61d7f7fd8f90a065f090de17c25c10b35348c82aee9a64f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-56-6","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":56,"verse":6,"english":"Ever virtuous, you, that have seen both the virtuous and the vicious, although aggrieved, ought not to say anything unpleasant to me who am weighed down with woe.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.892,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-62-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2056006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"093205e81e4976c192f1eba43fd0b08eb384bde988c5c99813cafe4ef678823d","compact":"94742d0729799f8c25e19f9a96e8a0bc10b48c405435446923734ae043947fb8","nasal":"94742d0729799f8c25e19f9a96e8a0bc10b48c405435446923734ae043947fb8"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-56-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":56,"verse":7,"english":"Having heard these piteous words of the distressed king, Kausalyā uttered words even as a water-way lets out fresh accession of rain.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.7,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-62-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2056007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0dce3577a5d1e749fa31ab80681079e30cab8c25c329fa0e3c194cd6a719a72a","compact":"663389e4133a636e5d97dfb203d6c4667fdcb49cd503236febf18dca4f1f9c1c","nasal":"663389e4133a636e5d97dfb203d6c4667fdcb49cd503236febf18dca4f1f9c1c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-56-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":56,"verse":8,"english":"And weeping, she drew on her head the joined hands of the king resembling lotuses; and then flurried spoke these words hurriedly informed with extreme affection.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.76,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-62-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2056008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"013f79a664e36ace2c1f5b17849c6475a646129900bd4968c45f182a39e2b4ce","compact":"7dff1851f534141d043b03a269df3ec7ff1ce0638a9a07c279348264513c44ed","nasal":"108d23d9ff87ed2d0c380437e02f0c2f90b5e90a18898bfafdec4b4921a40471"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-56-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":56,"verse":9,"english":"Be you propitious; I beseech with (bended) head. I bow to you, falling on the ground. O reverend one, besought by you, I shall be undone. I do not deserve to be forgiven by you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.729,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-62-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2056009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c7a1fc7e71e08609accc682ec512e535c2fb827fc251d6287bf01174c3bc750b","compact":"8a573b342771278fca879aab5ab5036ecb206da73def027a570c57dae35508c1","nasal":"3635c6a34d58a105d2aeca89b8db4e1a0763679a9f9878d567897ac5e185bd0a"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-56-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":56,"verse":10,"english":"She cannot be reckoned a gentlewoman, who is propitiated by her intelligent husband, worthy of being extolled in both worlds.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.705,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-62-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2056010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3e3a136bdcc1d5d23d84e7f1ec3e838273b3c6eec4bf2e7fe3ac8878364a4f56","compact":"789cc0f605f85548bf59466f0c037957927d13a1a4094911f46e914a0b15894f","nasal":"789cc0f605f85548bf59466f0c037957927d13a1a4094911f46e914a0b15894f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-56-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":56,"verse":11,"english":"I know duty, O righteous one; I know that you are truth-telling. And it is because I was exceedingly distressed on account of my son that I spoke harshly to you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-62-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2056011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5918d87d19ef6f58352c41079ca819df622f79ba0618beb2b6c3b8eb9e54ba26","compact":"29a76c168c77b969cc0af5c022be718b0919a837e2f24f6b0f03c3fc094933cd","nasal":"e8830687c889aa7e7e63318889cf01cb027afb1fb047d26bacd50660c6500484"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-56-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":56,"verse":12,"english":"Sorrow destroys patience, sorrow destroys knowledge of the scriptures, sorrow destroys every things; there is no enemy like to sorrow.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-62-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2056012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e43f1321e2fe7d0974c7c287b2b4e9ac23daf455fff460a64c2b0c7651ef660f","compact":"3d31227316fe0b66d940c4f9273b3185bf14d449ce4631452f195dda16ec81fa","nasal":"3d31227316fe0b66d940c4f9273b3185bf14d449ce4631452f195dda16ec81fa"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-56-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":56,"verse":13,"english":"One can falling down bear ever beating from an enemy; but one cannot falling down bear ever so little sorrow.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.719,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-62-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2056013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"af64499c93c39627f19756950b47858803620e2c94670edfed3c15bfb241fec6","compact":"93560ede0e05ee8ad4e98411a50e82b251d6aa81ab6c824dc1ee62b852008a27","nasal":"93560ede0e05ee8ad4e98411a50e82b251d6aa81ab6c824dc1ee62b852008a27"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-56-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":56,"verse":14,"english":"This is the fifth night of the banishment of Rāma, as calculated by me; and to me rendered cheerless by sorrow, this interval has assumed the proportions of five years.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.815,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-62-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2056014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0c76dccdf8526cc21158e56422597e2a70a0317c8d63544e7e9038f5de09d234","compact":"9adcbf7aa511622a0c02375887f13e39df510ca88a5d4d35a217480ebd8337cc","nasal":"99f472f2c1c9ac9a5b665dc6a60dd262bccdb49bbb657869836720985a878d61"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-56-15","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":56,"verse":15,"english":"And fostered by thought on my part, this grief increases in my bosom, like the mighty waters of the ocean increased by the vehement discharge of rivers.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.852,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-62-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2056015","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9ae25828264c64b17e5c5f4678761979aeae8236be2e80d998569f4856715a29","compact":"552facce9b53d5838c639db3549e681f43931fbda973fc44d1fbe40410a9e5b7","nasal":"a0d3cd704ae064002ab7cdd432d6a3abbb73c8bc3204c061d2ccb1d0fd97bb7d"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-56-16","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":56,"verse":16,"english":"As Kausalyā was thus speaking auspiciously, the rays of the sun grew milder, and the night arrived. Cheered up by the words of Kausalya, the king overcome by grief, felt the influence of sleep.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-62-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2056016","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"448f264d800cdece185ed3759dc87e66829179a4cc9be3064b9925714bf35b45","compact":"f4577c001d89f5a39e21495339075a688ff58bca53d4ed377573a06fa02e06b1","nasal":"b9c8b1c4beb94bbb3234099beaca1525f2d6318c42544892ba4a6686de846190"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-56-17","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":56,"verse":17,"english":"As Kausalyā was thus speaking auspiciously, the rays of the sun grew milder, and the night arrived. Cheered up by the words of Kausalya, the king overcome by grief, felt the influence of sleep.","alignment":{"type":